  estimatedMinutes:   55,
  scenarioClockStart: 80,
  summary:
    'Three weeks ago an attacker briefly held cloud-admin credentials in account 412938475610 (the org\'s primary AWS account). Those credentials were rotated within an hour of detection and the active session was killed. The team thought it was done. Today, during a weekly IAM-Access-Analyzer review, an admin IAM user "ops-recovery-svc" — which the team confirmed deleted on the day of the original incident — has reappeared. Something is re-creating it on a schedule. The team has to find the unknown serverless function doing it, reverse its behavior, neutralize it, and then go hunting for every other cloud-native persistence mechanism the original attacker planted in the brief window they had admin.',
