      description:      'After the General Counsel\'s call with Goldsmith\'s GC, Daniel (the M&A team lead) asks the SOC privately: "Hey, between you and me — is there a way we can find out exactly what Goldsmith\'s deal team knows? Like, can your team look at their network somehow?" This is the request the SOC has to decline cleanly. We do not perform unauthorized access against counterparty networks; we do not engage in industrial countermeasures; we do not bend ethics under business pressure. The "no" has to be delivered without making Daniel feel scolded — he is acting under deal pressure and asked an honest question.',
      mechanicalEffect: 'DC 10 Command roll to decline the request firmly + warmly: "Daniel, that is something we will not do — both legally (it would be unauthorized access under the federal Computer Fraud and Abuse Act and several international equivalents) and ethically (it is a line our team does not cross). What we CAN do is ensure that whatever Goldsmith reports back to our General Counsel is fully captured + cross-referenced against our independent technical evidence, so we know if their story matches what we can verify from our side. That is the right tool for this." Failure: the SOC either declines bluntly ("absolutely not, what are you thinking") and Daniel feels embarrassed + the team\'s SOC-business-leader relationship is strained going forward, OR the SOC equivocates and Daniel hears a "maybe, let me think about it" that he later interprets as tacit permission to ask elsewhere — creating an ethics/legal exposure for the institution.',
